---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Our Story | Mega Texas BBQ">
  <Header />
  <main class="bg-bg-light min-h-screen pb-24">
    <div class="relative bg-black text-white py-32 px-6 md:px-12 text-center overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
        <img src="/images/smoker.jpg" alt="Inside the Mega Texas BBQ Smoker" class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-80" />
      </div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 z-10 bg-gradient-to-t from-black via-black/60 to-primary-red/40"></div>
      <div class="relative z-20">
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-extrabold mb-6">OUR ORIGIN STORY</h1>
        <p class="text-xl opacity-90 max-w-2xl mx-auto font-medium leading-relaxed">
          From a gas station parking lot to a Texas Monthly Top 50 pit. This is how we brought real Texas BBQ to the Central Valley.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 mt-20 space-y-24">
      <section class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-primary-red uppercase tracking-tight">The Gas-Roots Beginning</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Mega Texas BBQ was founded in 2013 by Anthony "Mega" and Tasha Vallejo. The journey didn't begin in a state-of-the-art restaurant, but rather in a humble setup at an Arco gas station on McKinley Avenue in Fresno. 
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Anthony earned the nickname "Mega" due to his commanding physical stature and his time spent living in Texas. He returned to his native Central Valley with a burning passion: to recreate the authentic, low-and-slow Texas-style barbecue he had fallen in love with. For four years, operating out of that gas station, Mega Texas BBQ built a fiercely dedicated "gas-roots" following.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm transform rotate-2">
          <div class="aspect-square bg-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
            <img src="/images/gas-station.png" alt="Mega Texas BBQ at the Arco Station" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
          </div>
          <p class="text-center font-bold text-text-dark italic">"We didn't have a dining room, just good smoke and a loyal community."</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="order-2 md:order-1 bg-white p-4 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm transform -rotate-1">
          <div class="aspect-[4/3] bg-gray-100 rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-4">
            <img src="/images/staff carving beef.jpg" alt="Staff carving fresh smoked beef" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
          </div>
           <p class="text-center font-bold text-text-dark italic">Obsessing over every brisket to prove Fresno could stand with the nation's best.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="order-1 md:order-2 space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-primary-red uppercase tracking-tight">Putting Fresno on the Map</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            The turning point came when Anthony saw a national publication rank an Oakland competitor as California's top barbecue destination. That fueled a competitive fire. He elevated his craft, obsessing over every brisket, rib, and side dish to prove that Fresno could stand toe-to-toe with any BBQ joint in the nation.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            That relentless drive paid off. Mega Texas BBQ won the prestigious Best of Central California award, and in 2024, achieved the ultimate honor: being named one of the 50 best Texas-style barbecue joints in the entire country by Texas Monthly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="text-center bg-bg-alt p-12 rounded-3xl border border-gray-200 shadow-inner relative overflow-hidden">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0 opacity-10">
           <img src="/images/patio.jpg" alt="Mega Texas BBQ Patio" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
        </div>
        <div class="relative z-10">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-primary-red uppercase tracking-tight mb-6">Our Permanent Home</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-dark max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-8">
            Today, we are proud to serve our community from our permanent brick-and-mortar storefront in the Calwa/Winchell neighborhood at 3598 E. Butler Avenue. It's a welcoming neighborhood beacon where our smoky patio invites everyone to sit down and enjoy the fruits of our labor.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-text-dark max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-10">
            We even had the honor of serving comedian Bill Burr, who called our food the "best barbecue he's ever had" and highlighted our signature Texas Twinkie on his podcast.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
             <a href="http://megatexasbbq.square.site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-block bg-primary-red text-white px-10 py-4 rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:bg-red-700 transition-all shadow-md">
              Order Now
            </a>
            <a href="/menu" class="inline-block bg-white text-primary-red border border-primary-red px-10 py-4 rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:bg-gray-50 transition-all shadow-sm">
              View Menu
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>